brief:
The person tagged the bot in a reply. The post they tagged it in says:
@buildthis.bisks.net a website listing top 100 most downloaded crates.io packages that haven't been updated in over 3 years, titled "ape brain serum graveyard"

The thread it's replying to, oldest first (this is the context "this" refers to):
@aub.bsky.social: everybody should watch "colossus: the forbin project" before they're allowed to work on machine learning. it's a great educational exercise in why you don't build a radiation moat around a data center & then give the LLM running on that data center total control of your nuclear arsenal.
  [quoting @melaniemitchell.bsky.social: Worth revisiting this prescient paper from @mmitchell.bsky.social and others from @hf.co :  arxiv.org/abs/2502.02649 (link: https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.02649)]
@aub.bsky.social: this lesson generalizes in many ways to smaller autonomous agents responsible for, say, single grenades, but it's written in big text & simple words so computer scientists can understand the moral of the story.
@aub.bsky.social: if science fiction teaches us anything it's that you never give an ape brain serum and you never give a computer a gun
